    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368-a1">

                <pb facs="0484" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg416"/>

                <head> [Mem. from Mr. Williams.] </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 29, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Subsequent rumors indicate that the French are pressing on towards the capital of
                    Corea, and that it has been attacked and captured, and the king has fled. There
                    is very little doubt about the death of all the company on board the General
                    Sherman.” The Coreans decapitated them all” is the brief account which has just
                    been received.</p>

                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry D. Bellonet</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">French Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



